														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-479720">
									

<p>I decided to have this be the exception that proves the rule, as it were. (And I looked up that expression.) If there's anything that would unnerve an O5, I believe it would be an uncontainable SCP with infinite power. I wrote those two comments in a bit of a hurry: if you think they need a bit of rewording (O5-2 <em>is</em> a little hysterical in his use of formatting) then go ahead. IIRC, O5s have used extremely informal language in the past: I thought this was the norm.</p>
<p>I believe the English parlour and hamburger are both essential to 343: he is completely and utterly benign, or at least that's all he chooses to show us.</p>
<p>What I did was remove all traces of him <em>not</em> being so benign, so that all we have are suspicions. We can't even process the idea of an SCP with that much power that <em>isn't</em> a threat, and for good reason, considering all the harmful stuff we have. So we watch him very, very, carefully, and pray that he's only what he appears to be.</p>
<p>If we're to have an SCP <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">that's</span> may or not be God, then I think this is the only way we can really swing it.</p>

