			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-520467">
									

<p>Hmm. Now that I think about it, I'll agree with you that the O5 comments are a little heavy-handed. I was trying to alter the tone of the article significantly.</p>
<p>However, before my alterations, the article implied that SCP-343 was actively drawing people towards it, and even turning people into puppets. For example, Dr. Beck's "odd request", which was not especially odd at all and served only to imply weird goings-on. What I did was make him <em>more</em> harmless, and <em>more</em> ambiguous, turning down the sinister suggestions of mind-control to a single, limited example, and replaced them with a mere suspicion.</p>
<p>far2 is most likely not the one who wrote this article. If you'll take a look, the older SCPs were transferred to this wiki some time around the end of July 2008, and far2 is the admin who did most of it. As such, I don't believe we do know who originally wrote SCP-343. In any case, there was a significant recent backlash towards it, which is what inspired me to do what I considered to be some fixing.</p>

							</div>

								
					
