			<div class="content" id="post-content-520646">
									

<p>I would love to continue this discussion, but I worry that our current mode of point-by-point response would lead to rapidly-ballooning multi-page forum posts. I won't mind you changing the article back if you get support on the issue.</p>
<p>I will say that I believe Occam's Razor does a number on your "Dr. Whatever is fine and dandy and is just doesn't make friends easily" theory though, especially given the "confrontation" bit and the part about no records of him ever having existed.</p>
<p>Frankly, I think the entire data-corruption thing is silly. Anyone trying to alter the records would do a better job than that, and anyone seeing the report in such a state would fix the corruption immediately. It's just unprofessional and a clumsy way to add mystery.</p>

							</div>

								
